{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>עקב</b>, צנים — two joined things." "<b>עקב</b> — the end of humility brings about fear of HaShem, as in: one commandment draws [after it] another commandment, and brings about for the humble one wealth and honor [and] riches, or that others will honor him." "<b>And life</b> — that his days will be lengthened."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {1 "The string עושר וכבוד ממון is read as three nouns: wealth, honor, riches. Reading ממון as an independent noun parallel to עושר, though the syntactic flow is compressed."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:08.751030688Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}